Save-guard caller list, re-derived AT HEAD (correction evidence for 0d734c0)
============================================================================

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. 0d734c0's message claimed "TRACKED files at HEAD already
named them" and then listed four call sites. Two of those four were read out of
the WORKING TREE, not out of HEAD. Both files are still ` M` (other lanes'
in-flight edits), so their line numbers describe a state git does not carry.
0d734c0 is a permanent record and cannot be rewritten, so the corrected list is
recorded here and in the body of the commit that adds this file.

FRAME. "HEAD" below means 800f1a9 -- the commit 0d734c0 was made against, i.e.
the tree as it stood BEFORE the four modules were committed. That is the only
frame in which the question "would a clean clone build?" is meaningful.

Every line below is reproducible with git alone; no working tree is consulted.


--- WRONG IN 0d734c0: cited, but not present at HEAD ------------------------

  $ git show 800f1a9:client/src/anim.rs | grep -c cutscene
  0

    0d734c0 cited "client/src/anim.rs:40 use crate::cutscene::{..}".
    anim.rs at HEAD does not mention cutscene ANYWHERE. Line 40 exists only in
    the modified working-tree copy.

  $ git show 800f1a9:client/src/shot_main.rs | grep -n '#\[path'
  15:#[path = "hero.rs"]
  22:#[path = "vfx.rs"]

    0d734c0 cited "client/src/shot_main.rs:22,28 #[path] characters/equipment".
    At HEAD shot_main.rs includes hero.rs and vfx.rs and nothing else; line 22
    is vfx.rs, not characters.rs. The characters/equipment includes exist only
    in the modified working-tree copy.

    CONSEQUENCE: the claim that voxelforge_shot was uncompilable at HEAD is
    WITHDRAWN. It built fine. Only two bins were actually broken (below).


--- RIGHT, AND UNDERSTATED: what HEAD really required -----------------------

  $ git show 800f1a9:client/src/main.rs | grep -nE '^mod (characters|equipment|cutscene);'
  14:mod characters;
  16:mod cutscene;
  24:mod equipment;

  $ git show 800f1a9:client/src/char_shot_main.rs \
      | grep -nE 'mod (characters|equipment);|path = "(characters|equipment)\.rs"'
  22:#[path = "characters.rs"]
  23:mod characters;
  25:#[path = "equipment.rs"]
  26:mod equipment;

    0d734c0 cited only main.rs:16 for main.rs. main.rs at HEAD declared all
    THREE modules, so the game binary was missing three files, not one. The
    original message understated its own strongest evidence while overstating
    the weak part.


--- enemy_shot_main.rs: no HEAD caller at all, and that is expected ---------

  $ for b in main shot_main perf_main audio_proof_main char_shot_main \
             enemy_ai_proof_main vfx_proof_main; do
      git show 800f1a9:client/src/$b.rs | grep -c 'enemy_shot_main'
    done
  (all zero)

    Nothing #[path]-includes a bin root. enemy_shot_main.rs becomes a build
    input only through the [[bin]] entry in client/Cargo.toml, which was
    uncommitted until 0d734c0 landed it. 0d734c0 described this correctly.


--- CORRECTED VERDICT ------------------------------------------------------

  Unbuildable from a clean clone at 800f1a9:
    voxelforge            main.rs:14,16,24  -> characters.rs, cutscene.rs, equipment.rs
    voxelforge_charshot   char_shot_main.rs:22-23,25-26 -> characters.rs, equipment.rs

  NOT broken at 800f1a9 (0d734c0 wrongly said it was):
    voxelforge_shot       includes only hero.rs + vfx.rs at HEAD

  The save-guard commit's PURPOSE is unaffected: two shipped bins genuinely
  could not build, ~3.5k lines were reachable by `git clean -fd`, and the
  manifest still had to land with the file it names. Only the evidence list
  was wrong, and it was wrong in a way that inflated the blast radius.

LESSON. A line number is meaningless without the tree it was read from. Six of
the eight files in play here are ` M`, so `grep client/src/...` answers a
different question than `git show HEAD:client/src/...` -- and only the second
one belongs in a commit message.
